{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4cee8fa854ba3cbfb842c4159bb13426c5c7e4ad6937d0f73c487206e823fec5","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM prompt caching warning system","key_entities":["warn_if_cache_ineffective","src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","cache_read_tokens","cache_write_tokens","input_tokens"],"problem_keywords":["cache","warning","false positive","caching ineffective","prompt caching","cache floor"],"propositions":["warn_if_cache_ineffective fires on every call with input_tokens below 4096 even when zero cache counters is expected and correct, causing alarm fatigue","the warning cannot distinguish between a cacheable prompt that failed to cache (real defect) and a sub-floor prompt that never caches (expected), making both indistinguishable in logs","CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS = 4096 floor constant is defined only in pass1.py but warn_if_cache_ineffective in structured_run.py has no knowledge of it, creating inconsistent behavior across the codebase","the predicate must gate the warning on input_tokens >= CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS to suppress false alarms below the floor while preserving detection of genuine caching failures above it"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787339101491084001,"uuid":"a44fe286-8ec9-42db-b4fa-85c60b564744"}